[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SchematicLab prototype requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-WEB-001
TITLE: Embedded electronics lesson
STATEMENT: >>>
The prototype shall run in a browser from static files and expose a voltage-divider lesson that can be embedded in an iframe.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-MODEL-001
TITLE: Parts and electrical identity
STATEMENT: >>>
The schematic shall store typed part instances and wires between explicit terminals independently of symbol artwork. Wire crossings and coincident drawing coordinates shall not create electrical connections.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-EDIT-001
TITLE: Bounded editing
STATEMENT: >>>
A learner shall be able to place supported parts, wire terminals, change component values, delete a selected part and its incident wires, and reset the lesson. Rejected connections and invalid values shall leave the document intact.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-LESSON-001
TITLE: Voltage-divider feedback
STATEMENT: >>>
The prototype shall report the analytical output voltage of a valid two-resistor divider. Incomplete or unsupported circuits shall receive feedback and shall not display a computed voltage.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-PLOT-001
TITLE: Probe and DC sweep plot
STATEMENT: >>>
The lesson shall label the voltage probe at its terminal and plot its voltage against the input in volts over a 21-point analytical DC sweep. Invalid circuit topology shall suppress the trace and report the missing result.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-CAT-001
TITLE: Generic component library
STATEMENT: >>>
The browser palette shall expose grouped and searchable generic symbols with explicit ordered terminal names and geometry. Placing a symbol shall give it a unique instance ID. The inspector shall distinguish symbols that can be evaluated in the lesson from symbols available for placement and wiring.
<<<
